mn86:18.31 starts: Some tame with a blunt stick,
mn86:18.32 starts: with hooks, & with whips
mn86:18.33 starts: But without blunt or bladed weapons
mn86:18.34 starts: I was tamed by the one who is
mn86:18.51 starts: They’re addicted to heedlessness
mn86:18.52 starts: —dullards, fools—
mn86:18.53 starts: while one who is wise
mn86:18.54 starts: as his highest wealth.
mn128:6.17 starts: Hostilities aren’t stilled
mn128:6.18 starts: through hostility,
mn128:6.19 starts: Hostilities are stilled
mn128:6.20 starts: This, an unending truth.
mn130:30.7 starts: But those here who are good,
mn130:30.8 starts: people of integrity,
mn130:30.9 starts: aren’t heedless
mn130:30.10 starts: of the noble Dhamma—ever.
